<title>GERMANY: Germany may offer guarantees for China dam project.</title>
<headline>Germany may offer guarantees for China dam project.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's government is ready to provide 1.3 billion marks ($833.4 million) worth of export guarantees to help finance the construction of China's controversial &quot;Three Dams&quot; hydroelectric project, a newspaper reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Citing a confidential paper reviewed by parliament's budget committee, the Hannoversche Allgemeine newspaper said the state guarantees would cover supplying 14 German-made turbines and 14 generators for the project.</p>
<p>An additional 72 million marks would be provided to cover delivery of 11 German cranes.</p>
<p>The newspaper said that environmentalists have criticised the project, which would create a lake 600 km (375 miles) long and flood 21 towns and villages. The Three Dams project is due for completion in 2010 at a cost of 100 billion marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150 ($ = 1.559 German Marks)</p>
